-From a0ac02fbd8485286e2c0643c352b43b81c63c468 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:35:12 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] fix(truth): the audit script was reporting failures it never
- established
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Two bugs, both of which made `pnpm truth` say "this did not ship" about
-things that had shipped. Found by running it against 96dc93a from a sandbox
-and getting twelve discrepancies on a site that serves all twelve.
-
-1. SIGPIPE UNDER PIPEFAIL — the serious one
-
-   `set -o pipefail` is on, and both pipe helpers ended in `grep -q`. grep -q
-   exits the instant it matches, which closes the pipe under `git show` and
-   `curl`, raises SIGPIPE, and returns 141. pipefail then reports 141 as
-   failure. It only fires when the producer is still writing, so it passed on
-   vercel.json (a few lines) and failed on lib/guides.ts (750 lines) — and on
-   every real HTML page, which is to say on every live check in the file.
-
-   A "not found" that is really "found it too quickly" is the worst shape a
-   check can take, because it is indistinguishable from the thing it is
-   supposed to detect. Both helpers now count matches, which consumes the
-   whole stream. Demonstrated before and after:
-
-     git show origin/main:vercel.json          | grep -q '"has"'   → 0
-     git show origin/main:apps/web/lib/guides.ts | grep -q seoTitle → 141
-
-2. NO CONTROL PROBE
-
-   Every live check is a curl, and a curl that cannot reach the network fails
-   identically to one that reached a deploy missing the artefact. Both
-   rendered as a red NO under the line "it shipped but the deploy does not
-   serve it". The old-domain row went further and printed "NOT consolidated,
-   still splitting authority" off an HTTP 000.
-
-   The site root is now fetched before anything else. If it cannot be reached,
-   the network is the finding: every live row reads UNREACHABLE, the
-   old-domain row says "no conclusion", and the verdict states plainly that
-   the live column was not established. This is the same fix, for the same
-   reason, as the control probe already in verify-domain-redirect.mjs — which
-   is the part that stings, because it was written in this repository for this
-   exact failure and not carried across.
-
-   --quick had a quieter version of the same lie: it makes no live request and
-   still printed "present in the repo and live". Fixed.
-
-Also: --selftest, asserting each helper on a small input, a large input and a
-miss. The SIGPIPE bug survived a full patch cycle precisely because it needs
-an input big enough that the producer is still writing — the shape of bug
-nobody reproduces by hand. `in_repo` normalised to 0/1; `git cat-file -e`
-exits 128 on an absent path, which worked by accident wherever the test was
-"non-zero".
-
-And four rows for what patch 81 shipped: the head-term rail (probed on a
-service-area page, because if it is missing from that template it is missing
-from 32 pages at once), /team, the guide keyword titles and the guide FAQPage.
-
-This is the seventh instance in this repository of a check that reports a
-verdict without doing the work — F-117, F-149, F-166, F-177, F-192, F-203.
-The pattern is always the same: the check's success path and its
-cannot-run path are the same code path. Record as F-204.
-
-Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ur5ARwToq5LHXqViEAJH9W
